# Destination File
codeClear.ts
# Dependencies
# Output
export function clearCodeInLlmResponse(llmResponse: string) : string
# Options
Active=False
# Import prompts
# Prompt
Cases:
1. If the response contains one or more Markdown code blocks (```),
extract and return only the content inside the code block(s), 
without the Markdown markers.

Ignore any text lines outside the code blocks.

Example:
=========
Some line before code
Line 2 before code
```Python
def hello():
  print("Hello world")
```
Some text after code
Line 2 after code
========

Result:
========
def hello():
  print("Hello word")
========

2. If the response does not contain any Markdown code blocks,
return the full response unchanged.

Guidelines: Please don't use regular expressions.
Instead, create an algorithm with a loop over code lines.
example:
```typescript
...
if(line.trim().startsWith(`\`\`\``)) {
...
```